    "created_at": "2016-08-25T02:20:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-25T02:20:56Z",
    "body": "I don't have much background on this issue, please forgive me to ask:\n1. The content model of `rp` is phrasing content today.\n2. The rendering section has the following text for ruby:\n   \n   > User agents that do not support correct ruby rendering are expected to render parentheses around the text of rt elements in the absence of rp elements.\n3. Somehow this conflicts with `innerText` getter spec, and changing the content model of `rp` to text can solve.\n\nCould you mind to explain why 3 conflicts with 2?\n\nI suppose this is rarely used, so changing to text would be ok, but I'd like to understand what it is conflicting with, and wonder maybe somehow solving the issue it is conflicting with could be better.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/242263939/reactions",
