    "created_at": "2016-08-25T08:36:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-25T08:36:19Z",
    "body": "(2) doesn't conflict.\n\nThe issue is this: given the markup\n\n```\n<ruby> x <rp><span>(</span></rp> <rt>y</rt> <rp><span>)</span></rp> </ruby>\n```\n\n`innerText` does not include the parentheses as it is specified right now (and implemented in Gecko), because the Text nodes \"(\" and \")\" are in a display:none subtree and their parents are not an `rp` element.\n\nThe algorithm _could_ be changed to check for `rp` ancestors instead of parent, but that would be a complication for something that seemingly no Web page uses. (I couldn't find any instance of elements in `rp` in httparchive.)\n\n_Or_ the algorithm could be changed to always include \"(\" and \")\" around `rt` and ignore `rp`, then this would be a non-issue. But there are some pages that use other characters than those, and it still seems like a good change to only allow text in `rp` since there is no known use case for using anything else.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
