    "created_at": "2016-08-27T15:52:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-27T15:52:55Z",
    "body": "Thank you, now I understand the situation, and now I read the [spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#the-innertext-idl-attribute). I neglected to search for the spec, somehow I thought this was a non-standard feature, sorry about that.\n\nI didn't know this `display: none` difference between `innerText` and `textContent`, nor this nice little feature for `rp`.\n\nHad we considered removing this nice little feature for `rp` when 3 out of 4 browsers don't implement as far as I [tested](http://output.jsbin.com/kasaqo)? I understand it's a nice feature though.\n\nI'm still fine either way. A little worried if it requires a change to the parser implementation, thank you for clarifying that it's not the case.\n\nI mildly prefer removing the `rp` logic, but fine to change the content model, up to you.\n\nFYI, the most of HTML ruby usage today is in EPUB. EPUB has a validation tool called `epubcheck`, I'm not sure if it checks DTD for XHTML or not, nor if this change results in the change to DTD, but many stores such as Apple iBooks does not accept content that fails `epubcheck`, so it's a small possible risk.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
